<title>GERMANY: German cocoa imports lower in September.</title>
<headline>German cocoa imports lower in September.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>German cocoa bean imports from third countries were 223,629 tonnes in January -September 1996, up on the year-earlier level of 209,602, but imports in September were sharply lower, official data showed.</p>
<p>September imports were 21,513 tonnes after 35,264 tonnes a year earlier and compared with August imports of 44,379 tonnes.</p>
<p>September import value was 47.84 million marks against 82.27 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>Leading suppliers in the nine months were Ivory Coast with 128,995 tonnes, Ghana with 38,026, Indonesia with 21,997 and Nigeria with 11,749, excluding beans for toll grinding. --Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
